---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const description =
  'Important limits on using Clipwell: no platform affiliation, no legal advice, no guarantee of availability, and full user responsibility for downloads.';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Disclaimer"
  description={description}
  path="/disclaimer/"
>
  <p>
    This disclaimer explains the limits of the Clipwell service and the information published on this
    site. It applies alongside the <a href="/terms-of-service/">Terms of Service</a> and
    <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>. By using Clipwell, you accept these limits.
  </p>

  <h2>No affiliation with supported platforms</h2>

  <p>
    Clipwell is an independent utility. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, sponsored by or
    operated by Instagram, Facebook, YouTube, TikTok, Kick, Twitch, X or any other platform. All
    third-party names, logos and trademarks belong to their respective owners and are used only to
    identify the service a link comes from.
  </p>

  <h2>No legal advice</h2>

  <p>
    The content on Clipwell — including platform guides, copyright pages and FAQs — is general
    information, not legal advice. Copyright, privacy and platform rules differ by country and by
    situation. If you need certainty about a specific use, consult a qualified lawyer in your
    jurisdiction.
  </p>

  <h2>Your responsibility for downloads</h2>

  <p>
    You are solely responsible for the links you submit and the files you download. Clipwell does not
    determine whether you own a work, have permission to copy it or qualify for a legal exception.
    Public availability is not a licence. Do not use the service to infringe copyright, invade privacy
    or violate a platform’s terms.
  </p>

  <p>
    Downloaded files may contain personal information, third-party music or other material that is
    subject to additional rights. You are responsible for how you store, share or publish them.
  </p>

  <h2>No guarantee of availability or accuracy</h2>

  <p>
    Platforms change their pages, formats, authentication requirements and geographic restrictions
    without notice. Clipwell therefore cannot guarantee that a link will work, that a format will
    remain available, or that metadata will be complete or accurate. A successful extraction only
    reflects what the public source returned at that moment.
  </p>

  <p>
    The service may be unavailable during maintenance, capacity limits, network incidents or
    upstream outages. It may also refuse a request because of rate limits, file-size limits, legal
    requirements or security concerns.
  </p>

  <h2>No storage or backup service</h2>

  <p>
    Clipwell is not a cloud drive. Download files are held only long enough to deliver the request and
    are then deleted automatically. Do not rely on a job link as a permanent copy. If a download
    matters, save it to your own storage and back it up.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party links and content</h2>

  <p>
    The service links to or retrieves information from third-party platforms. Those platforms have
    their own content, terms and privacy practices. Clipwell does not control them, does not endorse
    the material they host, and is not responsible for their availability, accuracy or conduct.
  </p>

  <h2>Security and sensitive data</h2>

  <p>
    Do not send passwords, cookies, authentication tokens or private media through the downloader or
    in support email. The service is designed for public links. If you suspect a security issue,
    contact <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a> with enough detail to
    reproduce it, but do not include live credentials.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>

  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, the operator is not liable for losses arising from your
    use of the service, including copyright claims, account restrictions, data loss or damage caused
    by downloaded files. The full limitation is set out in the
    <a href="/terms-of-service/">Terms of Service</a>. Nothing here excludes liability that cannot
    lawfully be excluded.
  </p>

  <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>

  <p>
    If a page is out of date, a public link fails unexpectedly or you believe the service is being
    misused, contact <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>. For copyright
    complaints, use the <a href="/copyright-policy/">Copyright Policy</a> and
    <a href="/dmca-policy/">DMCA Policy</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
